<title>MOROCCO: Subscription for Moroccan silver mine closes.</title>
<headline>Subscription for Moroccan silver mine closes.</headline>
<dateline>CASABLANCA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public subscription for the privatised 20 percent state stake in Morocco's Imiter silver mine closed on Friday, a bourse official said.</p>
<p>Subscription for local and foreign investors were open on June 9. The official had no details about the preliminary results of the sale.</p>
<p>The privatisation ministry floated 20 percent of Imiter worth 130.3 million dirhams ($13.7 million), or 396 dirhams per share.</p>
<p>Imiter is expected to be listed on the bourse next week, the ministry said.</p>
<p>($1= 9.5 dirhams)</p>
<p>-- Newsroom +212-7 72 65 18</p>
